[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
t2-touchid needs:

 - libfprint built with its virtual devices (the VIRTUAL option of
   security/libfprint, on by default in Daemonarchy's ports tree);
 - the T2 link (cdce on USB 05ac:8233, ueN) up with IPv6 link-local and no
   DHCP: ifconfig ueN inet6 -ifdisabled auto_linklocal
   (Daemonarchy's daemonarchy-t2link does this);
 - fingers enrolled under macOS, and macOS logged into once since the T2
   last powered on (before that the Secure Enclave reports a locked,
   empty inventory).

It is disabled by default. To try it without changing PAM:

  service t2_touchid onestart
  fprintd-list <user>

To use it at boot, set t2_touchid_enable="YES" (and t2_touchid_bind_user
to bind the macOS-enrolled fingers to an account) in /etc/rc.conf, then
add pam_fprintd to the PAM services that should accept a finger, before
their password module, for example in /usr/local/etc/pam.d/sudo:

  auth  sufficient  /usr/local/lib/security/pam_fprintd.so

The rc script runs fprintd itself with FP_VIRTUAL_DEVICE_STORAGE set
(t2_touchid_fprintd="YES"), because D-Bus activation cannot pass it.
There is no Escape key to cancel a scan on FreeBSD: a prompt ends when the
finger matches or after the 10-second match window.
EOM
}
]
